story += [p('A complete visual guide to building and operating agentic systems.','h2'),p('Muhammed Juned Alam<br/>From First Principles to Production'),Metrics([(str(q['pages']),'pages in one book'),('39','chapters reviewed'),('287','integrated visuals')]),Spacer(1,13),p('Local preparation is complete. Public-release approval remains pending.','h2'),p('The AI-assisted audit read all 39 chapters and 117 A/B/C visual labs. It corrected two newly reproduced technical defects, repaired references and added edition details, a corrections policy and an accessible companion download.'),table(['Completed here','Still required'],[['Source audit and focused copy corrections','Independent practitioner technical review'],['61 companion tests from the delivered attachment','Professional copyediting and target-reader pilot'],['Layout, links, font provenance and package checks','Author code-licence choice and final rights confirmation']],[254,254]),Spacer(1,13),p('<b>Your decisions applied:</b> the author biography is omitted; technical references are retained. Reader corrections go to juned.alam.dev@gmail.com.'),p('This report is supporting review material, not a second edition of the book. No reviewers were contacted and no public publication or submission occurred.','small')]
start('02 / CORRECTIONS','What changed and why')
story += [section('01  Duplicate evidence must not change ranking','Chapter 12 assigned ranks before skipping duplicate IDs. Repeated IDs could displace later documents and change reciprocal-rank fusion. The corrected listing deduplicates each result list first; an exact-listing regression verifies duplicate-invariant ordering.'),section('02  Invalid clocks cannot prove recovery','The capstone could report recovered when availability or the current clock was NaN. It now validates finite, nonnegative numeric times, rejects Boolean/null/string values and enforces start &lt; end &lt;= available. The separate 30-second watermark remains. Regression checks include boundaries and fractional seconds.'),table(['Location','Additional correction'],[['Chapter 28','Use the actual meets_quality_floor helper name.'],['Chapter 31','Explain preapproval callback bypass and enforce registry policy at tool exposure/execution.'],['Chapter 36','Name the model tier used at each cost stage.'],['Research 06 / Appendix E','Refresh AWS idempotency and Strands documentation URLs.'],['Front and back matter','Add version, corrections contact and update process; remove biography.']],[128,380]),Spacer(1,12),p('All prior chapter headings and diagram/check/exercise blocks were preserved. All 78 visual/research lesson bundles are retained; one source URL changed. Local grammar and analogy clarifications are detailed in the scoped audit reports.','small')]
start('03 / EXECUTION EVIDENCE','Test the files readers receive')
story += [p('The final PDF attachment was extracted into a new directory. Its 60 source/metadata files matched the working source, and its ZIP bytes matched the separate companion download. The six suites ran in clean, isolated environments established during this review.'),table(['Delivered suite','Passed','Evidence'],[['Durable harness','19','SQLite and real process-loss/restart'],['Retrieval lab','8','Fixed/adaptive lexical fixtures and metrics'],['Judge fixture','8','Injection/control pairs and grading outcomes'],['Runtime snippets','11','Actual exported local OpenTelemetry spans'],['Foundation snippets','6','Exact chapter listings and real MCP stdio'],['Graph capstone','9','LangGraph persistence, crash/restart and invalid clocks']],[155,55,298]),Spacer(1,12),p('<b>Total: 61 passed, zero skipped.</b> All 55 Python manuscript blocks parsed. Dependency installs and pip checks succeeded in fresh Python 3.12.14 environments on macOS arm64.'),section('Scope matters','The graph, MCP transport, SQLite and telemetry library paths execute locally. Business services and model behavior are fixtures. No live Temporal server, PostgreSQL deployment, cloud infrastructure or provider model was exercised. These outcomes are not model-quality benchmarks or production certification.'),p('Machine-readable commands, full test output, attachment hash and extraction path are in delivered_companion_verification.json. Requirements and lab-specific limitations travel with the companion.','small')]
start('04 / BOOK AND SOURCES','Preserve the reading experience')
story += [table(['Check','Result'],[['Content-unit integrity',f'{q["intact_page_units"]:,} intact page units; zero reported layout issues.'],['Diagram labels and navigation',f'{q["diagram_labels_checked"]:,} labels and {q["internal_links_checked"]:,} internal links checked; 198 index entries, zero fallbacks.'],['Page bounds',f'{b["words_checked"]:,} word boxes across {b["pages"]} pages; zero out-of-page words.'],['Visual proof','Representative changed pages, front/back matter and diagrams inspected after rebuilding.']],[165,343]),Spacer(1,10),p('Paragraphs, analogy cards, code units, exercises and diagrams with captions remain together. Longer sections continue at natural block boundaries. The PDF includes reading-order tags and figure alternatives; PDF/UA and assistive-reader interoperability are not certified.'),section('References remain part of the book','The final reachability pass found 143 unique URLs: 139 returned HTTP 200, two are intentional fictional domains, one ACM DOI returned 403 and EUR-Lex returned 202. Restricted responses are recorded as access limitations, not proof of invalid references. HTTP success does not verify a claim; scoped reports record primary-source spot checks.'),section('Artwork, fonts and rights','All 18 font-package provenance records matched their stored hashes; licence notices are retained. Technical illustrations are editable vectors. AI-generated cover provenance and prompts are preserved. The author/publisher still needs to confirm manuscript rights and applicable disclosure requirements. Companion code reuse terms are pending.'),p('The current PDF is a reading edition. A printer-specific interior/cover spread or validated EPUB requires a separate production pass for the chosen platform.','small')]
start('05 / PRACTITIONER REVIEW','A concrete review assignment')
story += [p('Proposed allocation: three practitioners with relevant current experience. Record identity, conflicts, exact version/hash, reviewed chapters, commands and unreviewed boundaries. These roles have not been assigned or contacted.'),table(['Reviewer scope','Questions that need evidence'],[['Chapters 1-13: foundations/RAG','Are analogies accurate? Do retrieval metrics, context budgets, row policies and duplicate handling behave as stated? Can the lab be reproduced?'],['Chapters 14-26: runtime/security','Do protocol/version claims match sources? Can authority, retries, approvals or telemetry leak across a boundary? Are diagrams consistent with code?'],['Chapters 27-39: production','Do costs and quality gates recompute? Does restart preserve effect identity? Is recovery distinguished from an accepted write? Are integration limits explicit?']],[179,329]),Spacer(1,12),section('Review each learning unit','Check objective, explanation, analogy and its limit, diagram actors/arrows/units, prediction answer, worked arithmetic, code contract, source and prerequisite. Try counterexamples and malformed evidence instead of relying only on passing tests.'),section('Close findings with evidence','Critical and major issues must be corrected and independently rechecked. Minor issues need an editorial disposition. Use feedback_template.csv for version, location, observed/expected behavior, severity, evidence, correction and retest. An empty issue list does not replace a signed review scope.'),p('Live Temporal replay/timers/cancellation and PostgreSQL tenant-isolation deployment remain follow-up integrations. Preserve their limitations unless new execution evidence supports stronger claims.','small')]
start('06 / EDITING AND READERS','Test understanding, not just code')
story += [section('Professional copyedit','Harmonize US English while preserving literal code/status values and official titles. Check terminology, acronym introductions, units, denominators, analogy limits and source dates. Keep proposed, approved, executed and verified distinct. Preserve technical prerequisites when reducing repetition.'),p('Suggested reader pilot: six people, two for each route. Use participant IDs and record experience. Allow 60-75 minutes; record all hints and undocumented setup steps. This is qualitative feedback, not a statistical study.'),table(['Time','Reader task'],[['5 min','Find the contents, visual route, technical references and corrections contact.'],['15 min','Read an assigned concept and A/B/C labs. Explain the analogy, identify a limit, trace a change and predict before opening the answer.'],['25 min','Run one guided task: durable harness, fixed/adaptive retrieval, or graph capstone. Explain the result and failure boundary.'],['10 min','Use an index/answer link, inspect a diagram at zoom and in grayscale, and flag confusing page transitions.'],['10 min','Describe unclear or repetitive material and submit one practice correction report.']],[67,441]),Spacer(1,10),section('Proposed acceptance targets','Both readers on each route complete its core task without undocumented prerequisites. No severe misunderstanding about authority, evidence or recovery remains. Every reproducible navigation/setup defect is logged. Revise and retest a failed route with a fresh reader.'),p('The detailed moderator script, copyeditor style brief, severity rubric and sign-off form are in REVIEW_HANDOFF.md. No participant results are fabricated or implied.','small')]
start('07 / RELEASE GATE','The next decisions are explicit')
story += [table(['Owner / step','Required evidence before release'],[['Author: code terms','Choose the companion reuse licence. Replace LICENSE_STATUS.txt and synchronize PDF, metadata and ZIPs. No MIT grant is currently included.'],['Practitioners','Signed scopes and closure evidence for every critical/major technical finding.'],['Copyeditor and pilot readers','Completed editorial pass, recorded pilot outcomes and targeted retests.'],['Author / publisher: rights','Confirm underlying manuscript rights, quotations, artwork provenance and the selected platform’s disclosure requirements.'],['Production owner','Approve the final proof and format-specific export. Record matching book, companion and source hashes. Refresh marketing page counts before launch.']],[163,345]),Spacer(1,12),section('Version and correction policy','Keep this file set as 1.0-rc.1. Increment the candidate version for review revisions; record a public release date only when publication occurs. Errata identify chapter/section plus page because pagination can move. Update examples and dependency guidance together.'),p('<b>Reader contact</b><br/><link href="mailto:juned.alam.dev@gmail.com" color="#006FB9">juned.alam.dev@gmail.com</link><br/>Subject: Agentic AI Engineering - correction'),p('Include version, chapter/section, printed page, the issue and supporting source or minimal reproduction. For code: Python/dependency versions, command, expected and observed output. Remove secrets and private data.'),p('Prepared materials: complete book, identical standalone companion ZIP, editable source ZIP and review packet with scoped audits, evidence JSON, feedback CSV and rights register. Human approval and a public release are separate next steps.','small')]
